WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.267 --> 00:00:04.933
When checkout breaks, the operator needs evidence and a repair they can trust.

2
00:00:04.933 --> 00:00:10.867
First Response keeps the conversation going while an independent agent investigates and tests the code.

3
00:00:12.533 --> 00:00:15.300
These controls change a real Python shop.

4
00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:20.167
In this incident, a payment timeout falls from three thousand milliseconds to three.

5
00:00:20.167 --> 00:00:26.467
Checkout probes fail, and Pydantic AI validates Gemini's diagnosis against the trace and source.

6
00:00:28.467 --> 00:00:31.333
Gemini derives three edits from the broken code.

7
00:00:31.333 --> 00:00:34.100
It never sees our library of authored fixes.

8
00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:40.633
Each candidate runs separately in a network disabled Modal sandbox, against one reproduction and twenty four

9
00:00:40.633 --> 00:00:42.700
unchanged regression tests.

10
00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:46.567
Here is the important result.

11
00:00:46.567 --> 00:00:51.433
The five second timeout fixes the reproduction, but breaks timeout enforcement.

12
00:00:51.433 --> 00:00:53.300
A real regression rejects it.

13
00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:56.400
Two other candidates pass all twenty five checks.

14
00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:58.967
The model does not choose the test results.

15
00:01:00.967 --> 00:01:05.867
The operator selects the three thousand millisecond repair and reviews its exact diff.

16
00:01:05.867 --> 00:01:10.067
Approval checks the active incident and the fingerprint of the original source.

17
00:01:10.067 --> 00:01:12.800
Stale results cannot authorize changed code.

18
00:01:14.567 --> 00:01:16.667
Approval saves the patch as data.

19
00:01:16.667 --> 00:01:19.567
Generated code still executes only in Modal.

20
00:01:19.567 --> 00:01:24.333
Fresh verification passes twenty five tests and all twelve checkout probes.

21
00:01:24.333 --> 00:01:27.833
The shop recovers, and the approved patch is downloadable.

22
00:01:29.733 --> 00:01:33.767
The missing coupon incident produces three distinct generated guards.

23
00:01:33.767 --> 00:01:35.033
All three pass.

24
00:01:35.033 --> 00:01:36.733
There is no staged loser.

25
00:01:36.733 --> 00:01:42.433
Both incidents use the same evidence, isolated execution, and human approval workflow.

26
00:01:42.433 --> 00:01:46.100
This is a controlled prototype, with a complete repair loop.

27
00:01:48.267 --> 00:01:53.467
The coupon incident was caused by a null error when evaluating cart dot coupon.

28
00:01:53.467 --> 00:01:58.633
The approved patch successfully passed reproduction tests and all checkout probes to resolve the issue.
